# .gitignore Quick Reference
#
# Syntax rules:
#   • Lines starting with '#' are comments; blank lines are ignored.
#   • Patterns are evaluated top-to-bottom; the last matching rule wins.
#
# Where a pattern matches — the slash rule:
#   • No '/' at all, or only a trailing '/'  = match at any depth.
#   • A '/' at the start OR in the middle    = anchored to the directory
#     containing this .gitignore file. So 'temp/' matches a temp directory
#     at any depth, but 'src/temp/' matches only src/temp/ at this level.
#
# Wildcards:
#   • '*'  = zero or more characters within one path segment.
#   • '?'  = exactly one character within one path segment.
#   • '**' = any number of directories ('a/**/b' also matches 'a/b').
#   • '!'  = negate (un-ignore) a match from an earlier rule.
#
# Common pattern meanings:
#   Pattern       Matches
#   -------       ----------------------------------------------------------
#   build         Any file OR directory named "build" at any depth.
#   build/        Any directory named "build" at any depth. Files named
#                 "build" are never matched by a trailing-slash pattern.
#   /build/       Directory named "build" at this level only.
#   *.log         Any file ending in .log at any depth.
#   src/**/temp/  "temp" directories under THIS level's src/ only — the
#                 middle slash anchors the pattern.
#
# The classic gotcha — you cannot rescue files inside an ignored directory:
#       logs/
#       !logs/important.log    # does NOT work; git never descends into an
#                              # excluded directory
#   Instead ignore the directory's contents and negate what you keep:
#       logs/**
#       !logs/important.log
#
# Debugging:
#   • `git check-ignore -v <path>` prints the exact rule (file and line)
#     that ignores a path, or prints nothing if the path is not ignored.
#   • check-ignore only sees active rules — if an expected pattern seems
#     missing, check whether its section below is still commented out.
#
# File organization:
#   • The active rules at the top are starter defaults for common OS and
#     editor noise, IDE state, and developer-tooling local state. Review them
#     during customization and remove or revise rules that do not fit.
#   • Language-specific rules follow as OPTIONAL sections whose lines are
#     commented out, so they are inert until activated. To activate a
#     section, remove the leading '# ' from every line below its banner —
#     "uncomment the Java section" is enough for a coding agent. Delete
#     sections the project will never use.
#   • Activate and delete optional sections only as whole sections. Each
#     is self-contained, so a '!' rescue rule is never separated from the
#     rule it rescues.
#   • In a repository with several languages, a section can instead be
#     extracted (uncommented) into the language directory's own .gitignore.
#     Git scopes per-directory files to their subtree, so one language's
#     rules cannot affect another's files.
#   • For a language without a section here, start from the matching
#     template at https://github.com/github/gitignore, drop patterns the
#     active rules already cover, and prefer anchored or distinctively
#     named patterns over broad common-word directory names such as bin/
#     or build/.

# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  Operating system noise
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### macOS ###
.DS_Store
._*
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
# 'Icon?' stands in for the untypeable 'Icon' + two CR characters; it
# also matches five-letter names starting with "Icon", such as "Icons".
Icon?
.DocumentRevisions-V100
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
.fseventsd
.TemporaryItems

### Windows ###
Thumbs.db
Thumbs.db:encryptable
ehthumbs.db
ehthumbs_vista.db
[Dd]esktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
*.stackdump

### Linux ###
.fuse_hidden*
.directory
.Trash-*
.nfs*

# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  Editor temps, logs, archives, secrets, and local scratch
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### Editor temps ###
*~
*.swp
*.swo
*.tmp
*.bak
*.orig

### Logs and diagnostics ###
*.log
nohup.out

### Archives — committing one is usually a mistake; negate a specific
### file (for example !fixtures/sample.zip) when it is deliberate ###
*.zip
*.gz
*.tgz

### Secrets and local config ###
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

### Local scratch ###
/tmp/

# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  IDEs — keep only the editors your team uses
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### JetBrains (IntelliJ IDEA, GoLand, WebStorm, ...) ###
# JetBrains recommends committing .idea selectively; this template ignores
# it wholesale to avoid per-user churn and leaked data-source credentials.
.idea/
*.iws
*.iml
*.ipr
# IntelliJ writes build output to out/ when Gradle build delegation is off.
out/
!**/src/**/out/

### Eclipse and Spring Tool Suite ###
.apt_generated
.classpath
.factorypath
.project
.settings
.springBeans
.sts4-cache
bin/
!**/src/**/bin/

### VS Code ###
# Must be .vscode/* (not .vscode/) — git cannot re-include files inside an
# excluded directory, so the negations below only work with this form.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/tasks.json
!.vscode/launch.json
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/*.code-snippets
*.vsix

# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  Developer tooling — local-only state. The companion config files
#  (mise.toml, compose.yaml, AGENTS.md, ...) are meant to be
#  committed; only per-machine state is ignored here.
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### mise local overrides (mise.toml and .tool-versions are committed) ###
mise.local.toml
.mise.local.toml
mise.*.local.toml
.mise.*.local.toml

### AI coding agents — session/local state; shared instruction files
### (AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, .cursor/rules, ...) are committed ###
.claude/*.local.json
CLAUDE.local.md
.aider*

### Docker Compose local overrides — auto-loaded by `docker compose up`;
### delete these lines if the team commits a shared override instead ###
compose.override.yaml
compose.override.yml
docker-compose.override.yml
docker-compose.override.yaml

# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  Java / JVM (Gradle, Maven, Kotlin, packaging, crash dumps)
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### Compiled output ###
*.class

### Package archives ###
*.jar
*.war
*.ear
*.nar
*.car
*.sar
*.mar

### JVM crash/heap dumps ###
hs_err_pid*
replay_pid*
*.hprof

### Gradle ###
.gradle
.gradletasknamecache
build/
# Gradle expects the wrapper jar in version control.
!gradle-wrapper.jar
# Rescue real source dirs named "build" anywhere under a src/ tree; build
# tools never write output inside src/, so this cannot leak build output.
!**/src/**/build/

### Kotlin 2.0+ Gradle plugin project data (kotlinlang.org: do not commit) ###
.kotlin/

### Maven ###
# target/ is unanchored; when this section is active alongside the Rust
# section, it also covers Cargo's target/ directories.
target/
!**/src/**/target/
# Maven's wrapper defaults to script-only downloads, but the jar-type
# wrapper stays committable for networks that block the download.
!.mvn/wrapper/maven-wrapper.jar
dependency-reduced-pom.xml
pom.xml.tag
pom.xml.releaseBackup
pom.xml.versionsBackup
pom.xml.next
release.properties
buildNumber.properties
.mvn/timing.properties

# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  JavaScript / frontend (npm, Vite, Vue, Playwright)
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### Dependencies ###
node_modules/

### Bundler output (Vite) ###
dist/
# Rescue real source dirs named "dist" anywhere under a src/ tree.
!**/src/**/dist/

### Test artifacts (Vitest coverage, Playwright) ###
# The Playwright Java client writes its artifacts under the JVM build
# directory instead; these cover the JS test runner.
coverage/
/test-results/
/playwright-report/
/blob-report/
playwright/.cache/

### Tool caches ###
.vite/
.eslintcache
.stylelintcache
*.tsbuildinfo

